# Minimal Cisco vendor dictionary for ZeroRadius.
#
# This file ships in-repo so Cisco-AVPair based authorisation (e.g.
# `shell:priv-lvl=15` for CLI admin) works out of the box.  The
# `radius/Dockerfile` deliberately strips `dictionary.cisco*` from the
# upstream image so this file is the *only* Cisco dictionary the
# radius-server container ever sees; it is bind-mounted into
# `/etc/raddb/custom_dictionaries/` and the entrypoint regenerates the
# `$INCLUDE` lines at startup.
#
# If you need the full official FreeRADIUS Cisco dictionary, you can
# replace this file via either:
#   * the upload endpoint:  POST /api/v1/dictionary/upload
#   * the drop-in path:    replace this file and `docker compose restart radius`
#
# See `docs/modules/dictionaries.md` §3.1 and issue #76 for context.
#
# Vendor ID 9 (Cisco) is the IANA-assigned SMI Network Management
# Private Enterprise Code for Cisco Systems, originally registered
# in RFC 1700.  It is intentionally NOT listed in
# `_BUILTIN_VENDOR_IDS_FALLBACK` because the Dockerfile removes
# `dictionary.cisco*` from the image — the validator's
# `_get_builtin_vendor_ids()` only rejects vendor IDs that the
# running radius-server container actually ships with.

VENDOR    Cisco    9

BEGIN-VENDOR    Cisco

# Cisco-AVPair (type 1, string) — the canonical "privilege-level" /
# "shell:priv-lvl=15" attribute used for Cisco IOS / WLC / ASA
# administrative authorisation.
ATTRIBUTE    Cisco-AVPair    1    string

END-VENDOR    Cisco
